    isbefore: []  # 37e8
    duplicate_of: []  # 37e8
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 37e8
    pr_ref:  # 37e8
    description: "`tracker discuss <item-id> --ack-thread \"<msg>\"` fails with argparse \"unrecognized arguments: <first word of msg>\" when `--ack-thread` is positioned BEFORE the `message` positional. Must use `--ack-thread` AFTER the message: `tracker discuss <item-id> \"<msg>\" --ack-thread`.\n\nCause: argparse subparser ordering quirk — when a positional has `nargs=\"?\"` and an optional flag follows, argparse refuses to interleave. Workaround works but is non-obvious; the gate-message in `cli.py:781` even shows `--ack-thread \"<your reply>\"` (the broken order) as the suggested form.\n\nFix: either (a) update the gate-message in `cli.py:781` to print `\"<your reply>\" --ack-thread`, or (b) restructure the parser so order doesn't matter (e.g., make `--message TEXT` an optional flag and accept stdin). Option (a) is one line; option (b) is a small UX improvement.\n\nDiscovered while replying to four unread human-message threads on 2026-04-15. Three of four discuss calls failed silently before the order was corrected."  # 37e8
    fields: {}  # 37e8
